{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1163 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "60875a9cdbc352d68c454ef8e6b53fd30374a38e1f19126bbcab9608c604cdd9" :edb/db-before-t 1162 :edb/db-after-t 1163 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534475 50 #inst "2026-10-07T07:18:55.673Z" 13194139534475 true] [17592186152105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290316 13194139534475 true] [17592186152105 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290326 13194139534475 true] [17592186152106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290312 13194139534475 true] [17592186152106 1020 #edb/ref 17592186290319 13194139534475 true] [17592186152694 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534475 true] [17592186152694 1100 "Consider the line $y = 2x - 5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$?" 13194139534475 false] [17592186152694 1100 "Consider the line $y=2x-5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186152694 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=2x-5$ passes through the points $A(0,-5)$ and $B(1,-3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(5,0)$ and ${B}^{′}(4,2).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{2-0}{4-5}(x-5) \\\\ y & =-2(x-5) \\\\ y & =-2x+10 \\\\ 2x+y-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290312 1017 #edb/ref 17592186290313 13194139534475 true] [17592186290312 1089 "q-278618" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290312 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534475 true] [17592186290312 1100 "Consider the line $y=3x+5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-40.$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290312 1113 #uuid "525cff54-b46c-5657-adcf-4b43e73bacde" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290312 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=3x+5$ passes through the points $A(0,5)$ and $B(1,8)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -16 \\\\ 5 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-10,5)$ and ${B}^{′}(-16,12).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5 & =\\frac{12-5}{-16-(-10)}(x-(-10)) \\\\ y-5 & =-\\frac{7}{6}(x+10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-5 & =-\\frac{7}{6}(x+10) \\\\ 6y-30 & =-7x-70 \\\\ 7x+6y & =-40\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290314 13194139534475 true] [17592186290313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290315 13194139534475 true] [17592186290313 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534475 true] [17592186290313 1041 "field-1" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290313 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290314 13194139534475 true] [17592186290313 1110 #uuid "d8fb79a2-9b20-52bc-b059-160737f01f4a" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290314 1034 "7x+6y" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534475 true] [17592186290314 1111 #uuid "b90b6209-8665-5bca-a65f-38f2dcde1a08" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290315 1034 "6x+7y" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534475 true] [17592186290315 1111 #uuid "2bfa5bbc-041c-50c4-a6ab-8e28ee16640c" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290316 1017 #edb/ref 17592186290317 13194139534475 true] [17592186290316 1089 "q-281578" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290316 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534475 true] [17592186290316 1100 "Consider the line $x=4$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=16.$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290316 1113 #uuid "835dea08-d02f-5695-b6e8-88ac1d402393" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290316 1145 "First, notice that the line $x=4$ passes through the points $G(4,0)$ and $H(4,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $G$ and $H$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${G}^{′}(12,4)$ and ${H}^{′}(10,6).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${G}^{′}$ and ${H}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =\\frac{6-4}{10-12}(x-12) \\\\ y-4 & =-1(x-12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4 & =-x+12 \\\\ x+y & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290317 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290318 13194139534475 true] [17592186290317 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534475 true] [17592186290317 1041 "field-1" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290317 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290318 13194139534475 true] [17592186290317 1110 #uuid "f65cea3e-96ef-5463-a59e-68d962ad2ab7" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290318 1034 "x+y" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534475 true] [17592186290318 1111 #uuid "9424cfe2-6854-51f6-9245-1820857efc9d" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290319 1017 #edb/ref 17592186290320 13194139534475 true] [17592186290319 1089 "q-77776" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290319 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534475 true] [17592186290319 1100 "Consider the line $y=4x-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290319 1113 #uuid "8a72a83e-c00c-5e25-8dc9-1f34b89688c0" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290319 1145 "First, notice that the line $y=4x-1$ passes through the points $Q(0,-1)$ and $R(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $Q$ and $R$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${Q}^{′}(3,-2)$ and ${R}^{′}(-10,6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${Q}^{′}$ and ${R}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{-10-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+2 & =-\\frac{8}{13}(x-3) \\\\ 13y+26 & =-8x+24 \\\\ 8x+13y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290321 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290322 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290323 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290324 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186290325 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1041 "selection" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1104 #edb/ref 17592186290323 13194139534475 true] [17592186290320 1110 #uuid "625f4560-f4c4-52df-8e53-891c0a200f7d" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290321 1034 "13x+3y+2=0" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290321 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534475 true] [17592186290321 1111 #uuid "08fd19ea-c633-517a-b1c9-ee6f8212d9fe" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290322 1034 "8x+3y+12=0" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290322 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534475 true] [17592186290322 1111 #uuid "613759be-094a-5654-974d-97ea77254189" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290323 1034 "8x+13y+2=0" 13194139534475 true] [17592186290323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131